.nh
.TH "SYMVAULT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Symaira Vault" "Symaira Vault Manual"

.SH NAME
symvault-config-validate - Validate the configuration file


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsymvault config validate [path] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Validate the Symaira Vault configuration file for schema errors.

.PP
If no path is given, validates the default config at ~/.symvault/config.yaml.

.PP
When --fix is supplied, validation failures and recoverable load errors trigger
an interactive repair flow: deterministic defaults are offered for fields that
have safe replacements, and a manual $EDITOR session is offered as a fall-back.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--fix\fP[=false]
	interactively repair validation errors (requires a TTY)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for validate

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	output validation result as JSON (deprecated: use --output=json)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	When to emit ANSI color: auto, always, never

.PP
\fB--no-pipe-warning\fP[=false]
	suppress 'reading from non-TTY' warning when piping secrets

.PP
\fB--output\fP="text"
	Output format (text, json, yaml)

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	use a named vault profile

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress non-error output

.PP
\fB--theme\fP=""
	Color preset: default, highcontrast, colorblind (or SYMVAULT_THEME)

.PP
\fB--vault\fP="~/.symvault"
	path to the password vault


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBsymvault-config(1)\fP
